---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE_CONFIG } from '../../config';
import { BASE_URL as baseUrl } from '../../lib/url';

const pageTitle = `Privacy Policy | ${SITE_CONFIG.domain}`;
---

<Layout
  title={`Privacy Policy | ${SITE_CONFIG.author}`}
  description={`Privacy Policy and Web Tools Disclaimer for ${SITE_CONFIG.domain}. Learn how data is processed locally with zero tracking.`}
  activePage="privacy"
  headerTitle={SITE_CONFIG.domain}
>
  <div class="blog-intro">
    <h2 class="page-title">{pageTitle}</h2>
    <div class="blog-meta-date">First Published: 2026-11-07</div>
    <div class="blog-meta-date">Last Updated: 2026-11-14</div>

    <p class="blog-desc">
      This Privacy Policy and Web Tools Disclaimer outlines how personal information, web utilities, and technical data are handled across {SITE_CONFIG.domain}. We operate on a privacy-first principle: no third-party trackers, no unnecessary data acquisition, and completely local execution for interactive tools.
    </p>
  </div>

  <article class="prose max-w-none privacy-content">
    <section>
      <h3>1. Basic Policy on Personal Information</h3>
      <p>
        At <strong>{SITE_CONFIG.domain}</strong>, we recognize the paramount importance of personal information privacy and believe that the web should respect user autonomy. We strictly adhere to applicable data protection regulations and ensure that your browsing experience is transparent, safe, and respectful of your confidentiality.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h3>2. Acquisition & Processing of Information</h3>
      <p>
        As a static website hosted via GitHub Pages, minimal technical server access logs (such as public IP addresses, browser types, referral URLs, and access timestamps) may be generated at the infrastructure level purely for:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Monitoring network stability and detecting cyber security anomalies (e.g., DDoS attacks, abuse prevention).</li>
        <li>Ensuring reliable delivery of static assets and content over content delivery networks (CDNs).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not collect identifiable personal information (such as real names, government IDs, physical addresses, or financial details) during general browsing.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h3>3. Web Tools & Client-Side Processing (Zero-Server Architecture)</h3>
      <p>
        A core foundation of our <a href={`${baseUrl}tools`}>Web Tools</a> and <a href={`${baseUrl}playground`}>Interactive Playground</a> is <strong>client-side execution</strong>:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Local Execution:</strong> Calculations, encoders/decoders (Base64, URL encoding), UUID and NanoID generation, CSS clamp math, color contrast checks, code and JSON minification or beautification, JSON to TypeScript conversion, HEMIS credit module computations, and text conversions (such as the Uzbek reformed alphabet converter) run within your local browser engine via client-side JavaScript / Web APIs.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No Server Transmission:</strong> The text, tokens, source codes, formulas, or inputs you enter into the tools are <em>not</em> uploaded, transmitted, or logged to our servers or any third-party infrastructure.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Exception — PageSpeed Checker:</strong> The <a href={`${baseUrl}tools/pagespeed-checker`}>Website Speed &amp; Performance Checker</a> does not analyze the URL on our site. When you submit a URL, it opens Google's PageSpeed Insights (pagespeed.web.dev) in a new tab with that URL, and the request is handled by Google under <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Zero Persistent Cloud Storage:</strong> When you refresh or close the tab, temporary memory structures are automatically cleared by your web browser.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h3>4. Cookies & Client-Side Storage</h3>
      <p>
        We do not utilize marketing, advertising, cross-site profiling, or behavioral tracking cookies.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Local Storage:</strong> We use your browser's <code>localStorage</code> only for the following, and this data never leaves your device:
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Theme Preference:</strong> your Light or Dark mode choice (<code>theme</code>).</li>
            <li><strong>Credit Module Calculator:</strong> the subjects you entered and the selected calculation mode (<code>hemis_calc_subjects</code>, <code>hemis_calc_mode</code>), so they are still there when you return.</li>
            <li><strong>Playground Best Scores:</strong> your best Snake and Reaction Time results (<code>snake-best</code>, <code>reaction-best</code>).</li>
          </ul>
          You can clear this data at any time from your browser's site settings.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Third-Party Integrations:</strong> If you voluntarily engage with optional interactive features like GitHub Discussions / Giscus comments or external repository links, those third-party services operate under their own independent privacy terms.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h3>5. On-Site Search Privacy</h3>
      <p>
        Our search functionality is powered by <strong>Pagefind</strong>, a static search library designed for zero-backend privacy.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>All search indexes are downloaded statically by your browser and queried locally in memory.</li>
        <li>Your search queries, keywords, and keystrokes are never transmitted to any external telemetry or logging server.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="web-tools-disclaimer">
      <h3>6. Web Tools Disclaimer</h3>

      <p>
        The tools, calculators, converters, generators, and interactive demos on this website are provided <strong>&ldquo;as is&rdquo;</strong> and <strong>&ldquo;as available&rdquo;</strong> for informational, educational, and workflow-assistance purposes. By using any tool on this site you accept the terms described in this section in full.
      </p>

      <nav class="disclaimer-toc" aria-label="Web Tools Disclaimer sections">
        <strong>Table of Contents</strong>
        <ol>
          <li><a href="#disclaimer-general">General Terms</a></li>
          <li><a href="#disclaimer-liability">Limitation of Liability</a></li>
          <li><a href="#disclaimer-service">Service Conditions</a></li>
          <li><a href="#disclaimer-responsibilities">User Responsibilities</a></li>
          <li><a href="#disclaimer-third-party">Third-Party Services</a></li>
          <li><a href="#disclaimer-guidelines">Usage Guidelines</a></li>
          <li><a href="#disclaimer-final">Final Terms</a></li>
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <h4 id="disclaimer-general">6.1 General Terms</h4>
      <p>
        All web tools on {SITE_CONFIG.domain} &mdash; including but not limited to converters, formatters, validators, calculators, generators, minifiers, alphabet tools, and AI-powered utilities &mdash; are offered without warranties of any kind, express or implied. We make no guarantees regarding accuracy, completeness, reliability, or suitability for any particular purpose of the results they produce.
      </p>
      <p>
        These tools are personal projects maintained on a best-effort basis. We are under no obligation to fix bugs, add features, provide updates, or offer any form of technical support.
      </p>

      <h4 id="disclaimer-liability">6.2 Limitation of Liability</h4>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, {SITE_CONFIG.author} and {SITE_CONFIG.domain} shall not be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, special, or consequential damages arising from the use of &mdash; or inability to use &mdash; any tool, snippet, or interactive feature on this website, including but not limited to:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Data loss, corruption, or unintended disclosure.</li>
        <li>Incorrect computation results used in academic, financial, or production contexts.</li>
        <li>Service interruptions, API quota exhaustion, or third-party outages (such as background-removal APIs).</li>
        <li>Browser incompatibilities, crashes, or performance degradation on lower-specification devices.</li>
        <li>Any other direct or indirect losses arising from reliance on tool output.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Always independently verify critical results before using them for academic submission, legal purposes, production deployment, or financial decisions.
      </p>

      <h4 id="disclaimer-service">6.3 Service Conditions</h4>
      <p>
        We reserve the right to modify, restrict, or discontinue any tool at any time without prior notice. This includes changing processing limits, removing features, or taking tools offline temporarily or permanently. Tools that rely on external APIs (such as the AI Background Remover) are further subject to the availability, quota limits, and terms of those third-party services.
      </p>
      <p>
        Client-side tools (those with no network calls) run entirely in your browser and are not affected by server-side downtime. However, they depend on your browser version, available device memory, and local hardware capabilities.
      </p>

      <h4 id="disclaimer-responsibilities">6.4 User Responsibilities</h4>
      <p>You are solely responsible for:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Ensuring the content you upload or input (images, text, code) does not violate copyright, privacy rights, or applicable law.</li>
        <li>Verifying that tool output is correct and appropriate before using it in any consequential context.</li>
        <li>Complying with the terms of any third-party APIs or services that a tool connects to on your behalf.</li>
        <li>Keeping your browser and operating system reasonably up to date to maintain compatibility.</li>
      </ul>

      <h4 id="disclaimer-third-party">6.5 Third-Party Services</h4>
      <p>
        Some tools &mdash; such as the <a href={`${baseUrl}tools/bg-remover`}>AI Background Remover</a> and the <a href={`${baseUrl}tools/pagespeed-checker`}>PageSpeed Checker</a> &mdash; send data to external APIs in order to function. In those cases:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your uploaded images or submitted URLs are transmitted to the respective third-party provider (remove.bg, poof.bg, or Google PageSpeed Insights).</li>
        <li>Those providers&rsquo; own privacy policies and terms of service govern how they handle your data.</li>
        <li>We do not store, log, or retain any files or URLs you send through these tools on our side.</li>
        <li>API quotas are finite; if a service limit is reached the tool will display an informative error message.</li>
      </ul>

      <h4 id="disclaimer-guidelines">6.6 Usage Guidelines</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>Do not use these tools to process content that is illegal, hateful, or violates the rights of others.</li>
        <li>Do not attempt to abuse, overload, or reverse-engineer the tools or any APIs they depend on.</li>
        <li>Treat computed outputs as a starting point for review, not as authoritative final results.</li>
        <li>If you identify an error in a tool&rsquo;s logic, you are welcome to open a GitHub issue or pull request.</li>
      </ul>

      <h4 id="disclaimer-final">6.7 Final Terms</h4>
      <p>
        By using any tool on this website, you acknowledge that you have read and understood this disclaimer and agree to be bound by its terms. If you do not agree, please discontinue use of the tools immediately.
      </p>
      <p>
        This disclaimer may be updated periodically. The &ldquo;Last Updated&rdquo; date at the top of this page will reflect the most recent revision.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h3>7. Direct Inquiries & Contact Information</h3>
      <p>
        When you contact us directly via our <a href={`${baseUrl}contact`}>contact form</a>, email, Telegram, or GitHub:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>The contact form is processed by <strong>Formspree</strong> (formspree.io), a third-party form service that forwards your message to us. Your email address and message are sent to Formspree; Formspree's own privacy terms apply to that transfer. If spam protection is enabled, the form also uses <strong>Cloudflare Turnstile</strong>, which is governed by Cloudflare's privacy policy.</li>
        <li>We collect only the information provided voluntarily (such as your name, email address, and message body) to facilitate direct communication and respond to your inquiry.</li>
        <li>Your contact details are never sold, rented, or shared with third parties for commercial or promotional purposes.</li>
        <li>You may request the deletion of any inquiry records at any time by contacting us directly.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h3>8. Revisions to this Policy</h3>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy periodically to reflect new tools, changes in technical implementations, or relevant legal standards. The "Last Updated" date at the top will indicate when the most recent amendments were made.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="privacy-author-sign">
      Written by <a href={baseUrl}>{SITE_CONFIG.author}</a>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .privacy-content {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--text-copy, var(--text-body));
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .privacy-content section {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .privacy-content h3 {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-strong);
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
    padding-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .privacy-content h4 {
    margin-top: 1.4rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-strong);
  }

  .disclaimer-toc {
    margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--bg-code, var(--bg-soft));
    border-left: 3px solid var(--flora-orange, #b86752);
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .disclaimer-toc ol {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0 1.25rem;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .disclaimer-toc li {
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .disclaimer-toc a {
    color: var(--flora-orange, #b86752);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .privacy-content p {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .privacy-content ul {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem 1.25rem;
    list-style-type: disc;
  }

  .privacy-content li {
    margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
  }

  .privacy-author-sign {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
    text-align: right;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-soft);
  }

  .privacy-author-sign a {
    color: var(--flora-orange, #b86752);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
